edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265624 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186264739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265624 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d9c4e81f-33ab-54ad-9dac-693d04696388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1)\\,i+(\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2})\\,j-2yz\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "062ec003-5729-5fe0-9819-864cef26e212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266132 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{y}-{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int (-{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-y{z}^{2}+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=-y{z}^{2}+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2yz$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2yz & =-2yz+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+x-y{z}^{2}+C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132103" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ where $F(x,y,z)=(2x+y{e}^{z})\\,i+(x{e}^{z}+1)\\,j+(xy{e}^{z}-2z)\\,k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b7d90b3-0384-5231-a89f-b7683283ef28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266133 #edb/ref 1074 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+y{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2x+y{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{z}+1$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{z}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =x{e}^{z}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int \\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y+h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=y+h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xy{e}^{z}+y+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy{e}^{z}-2z$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{e}^{z}-2z & =xy{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =-2z \\\\ h(z) & =-{z}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{z}+{x}^{2}+y-{z}^{2}+C.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348898 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348898 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348898 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "32cd3a46-2070-5c04-b850-8162eeb789a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350047 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+y+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350047 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350047 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b4d8f137-d9d9-5d7a-bf57-3e496c94821f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350251 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350251 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350251 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd48e39f-f120-599e-9a6b-494a2b1af79a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350468 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+x+y+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350468 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350468 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e6d34f2d-177c-57dd-a130-fa54336633eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350519 #edb/ref 1080 "f(x,y)=4xy+xy+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350519 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/r